        "radioSource": "ESP32-S3-MINI-1 & MINI-1U datasheet v1.7: Bluetooth LE transmit 189 mA at 0 dBm and receive 93 mA (Table 6-5); Wi-Fi 802.11b transmit up to 355 mA peak (Table 6-4); external supply at least 0.5 A, 3.3 V",
        "sleepUa": 8,
        "cpuMa": 66.2,
        "radioMa": 93,
        "flashMb": 8,
        "notes": "The robot MCU when the ESP32-C3's pins run out: 39 GPIOs and four hardware pulse counters (PCNT) that decode both encoder channels in quadrature. ESP32-S3-MINI-1-N8: 8 MB flash, no PSRAM. Its USB Serial/JTAG controller on GPIO19 (USB_D-) and GPIO20 (USB_D+) programs it over USB-C with no bridge; UART0 on GPIO43/GPIO44. Strapping pins GPIO0, GPIO3, GPIO45, GPIO46. LCSC C2913206, a JLCPCB extended part.",
        "stock": null,
        "priceUsd": null,
        "inStock": null,
        "reason": "moved up from the ESP32-C3-MINI-1: 12 signals need pins free at reset (ENC_LA, ENC_LB, ENC_RA, ENC_RB for quadrature), it has 8; the ESP32-S3-MINI-1 has 31 and hardware quadrature counters (PCNT)"
